R.append(scoped_record('c0845','oa-seams-dole-denizens','Orion’s Arm — The Seams’ Dole-supported denizens','Orion’s Arm','A rudimentary universal floor across heterogeneous Seams economies',['web_fiction'],
 'Official Encyclopaedia Galactica Seams setting','Established Dole access under the Burdikeer','Living humans and active human-derived denizens arriving in and inhabiting the Seams',
 ['Every local market or government as identical','Crude support as luxurious Sephirotic abundance','Dormant files or repeated copies as extra residents'],
 'Every denizen arriving in the Seams receives Dole access to rudimentary food, shelter, clothing, transport and information. The card works through participating services, selected fabrication systems and housing authorities, and can even support stranded travelers. This is a durable technological basic-access mechanism across otherwise very different local economies. Guarantees are moderately strong for essentials, with low comfort, limited service participation and regional conditions preventing a claim of unrestricted abundance.\n\nThe Burdikeer is a constructed high-level tribemind assembled from archailect avatars and enforces the overarching framework. Effective authority over that common floor therefore lies near autonomous higher-machine control, while local ownership and politics remain diverse. A loose confederation does not automatically give ordinary humans final control of the sustaining system. Living humans and active human-derived residents are an explicit proxy within a broader population. Trade, exploration, care and industry continue, and a Dole card is not a census of people doing no useful work. Nonworking remains unresolved.',
 [-.55,-.9,None],[[-.85,-.05],[-1,-.6],None],
 ['Every denizen receives a documented basic-access card accepted by affiliated fabrication/services/housing; modest quality and local conditions qualify the guarantee.','The overarching floor is maintained by an independently governing constructed tribemind of archailect avatars; local political variety does not establish final human ownership.','No all-person useful-work census; receiving the Dole does not imply doing no trade, care, exploration or other useful work.'],refs,5,proxy=True))
